{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.1-4", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.1-4"}, "paraphrase": "Brahmā (Hiraṇyagarbha) asks Maheśvara about kaivalya; he is taught the path of the siddhas.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "teachers": ["tch:brahma", "tch:siva"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.12-14", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.12-14"}, "paraphrase": "Some say knowledge alone suffices; it does not bring perfection. Knowledge without yoga cannot liberate; yoga without knowledge is incapable; the seeker should practise both.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:yoga-jnana-samuccaya"], "disputes": ["dsp:yoga-or-knowledge-for-liberation"], "cross_refs": ["tea:yogatattva-upanisad:14-15"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.129-138", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.129-138"}, "paraphrase": "Mantra, laya, haṭha and rāja are four stages of one great yoga: mantra-yoga is the natural haṃsa repetition reversed as so'ham; haṭha the union of ha (sun) and ṭha (moon); laya the union of the knower of the field and the supreme; rāja the union of rajas and retas.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-yogas", "cpt:hamsa"], "paths": ["pth:yogatattva-four-yogas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.140-144", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.140-144"}, "paraphrase": "Two ways: the monkey's (gradual, completed in one body) and the crow's (the body perishes, he is reborn, meets a siddha guru and gains the fruit quickly).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:monkey-and-crow-paths"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.151-160", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.151-160"}, "paraphrase": "Powers are of two kinds: contrived (from mercury, herbs, rites, mantras — impermanent and weak) and uncontrived (arising spontaneously, permanent, in those free of vāsanās); they are to be kept secret, like tīrthas seen on the way. As goldsmiths test gold, the siddha is known by his powers; one without powers is still bound.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhis-in-yoga-upanisads"], "disputes": ["dsp:siddhis-sign-or-obstacle"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.161-163", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.161-163"}, "paraphrase": "Liberation is not the falling of the body; the yogin's body becomes Brahman like salt dissolved in water.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "body-layers"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.165-178", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.165-178"}, "paraphrase": "The body is Śiva's temple: ten doors, channels and winds; four seats (pīṭha) — Kāmarūpa at the mūlādhāra, Pūrṇagiri at the heart, Jālandhara at the throat, Uḍyāna between the brows.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:body-as-temple", "cpt:cakras"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.24-26", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.24-26"}, "paraphrase": "Even the knower needs the yoga of the body; bodies are unripe (apakva) or ripened (pakva) by the fire of yoga.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["body-layers", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:ripe-and-unripe-body"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.40-53", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.40-53"}, "paraphrase": "The yogin's body, burnt by the fire of yoga, is unseen even by gods; other knowers are 'lumps of flesh' reborn again, who meet a siddha and become yogins; knowledge comes from yoga in one birth; there is no path beyond yoga.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:ripe-and-unripe-body"], "disputes": ["dsp:yoga-or-knowledge-for-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.54-55", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.54-55"}, "paraphrase": "Merely thinking 'I am liberated' does not liberate at once.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.59-66", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.59-66"}, "paraphrase": "Mind is tied to prāṇa like a bird tied by a string; the only means is prāṇa. Partial knowledge brings great suffering; it is like crossing the ocean in an unbaked pot.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "practice"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.68-69", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.68-69"}, "paraphrase": "Yoga is the union of apāna and prāṇa, of rajas and retas, of sun and moon, of jīvātman and paramātman.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:bindu"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:2.14-19", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.14-19"}, "paraphrase": "Brahman has three bodies — gross (Vairāja), subtle (Hiraṇyagarbha, nāda) and supreme (being-consciousness-bliss); signs of the subtle are a lamp-flame, the moon, fireflies, lightning and stars.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:nada"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:2.2-3", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.2-3"}, "paraphrase": "This should be taught only to one who has served for twelve years.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:secrecy-and-eligibility"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:2.20-21", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.20-21"}, "paraphrase": "There is no mantra higher than nāda, no god higher than one's own Self, no worship higher than inner attention (anusandhāna), no happiness higher than contentment.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "original": {"text": "nāsti nādāt paro mantro na devaḥ svātmanaḥ paraḥ | nānusandheḥ parā pūjā na hi tṛpteḥ paraṃ sukham", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Īśādiviṃśottaraśatopaniṣadaḥ (Nirṇayasāgara collection of 120 Upaniṣads), South Indian recension carrying Upaniṣad Brahmayogin's opening maṅgala verses; e-text github.com/sanskrit/raw_etexts vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md", "licence": "text public domain; e-text licence unstated"}, "concepts": ["cpt:nada"], "practices": ["prc:nadanusandhana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:3.2-10", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "3.2-10"}, "paraphrase": "The power in the mūlādhāra as bindu sprouts as nāda (paśyantī), roars in the heart (madhyamā) and comes forth by the palate as vaikharī; from it arise letters, words, sentences, all mantras, Vedas, śāstras, purāṇas, poetry, languages and the seven notes; she is Sarasvatī; seeing her gives mastery of speech.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:levels-of-speech"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:4", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4"}, "paraphrase": "Non-dual teaching: the world is superimposed like a snake on a rope; one who makes even a little difference has fear.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:5.46-55", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5.46-55"}, "paraphrase": "Concentration on nāda gives far-hearing, on bindu far-seeing, on kāla knowledge of the three times, on another's body entry into bodies, on nectar freedom from hunger and poison, on the elements their mastery; bhāva is the cause.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhis-in-yoga-upanisads"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:5.56-59", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5.56-59"}, "paraphrase": "The guru is Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Sadāśiva; there is no difference between guru and Lord; one should never argue non-duality against the guru, but contemplate with devotion the non-duality of guru, god and self.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:5.62", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5.62"}, "paraphrase": "The yogin should not set his mind on powers.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "obstacles": ["obs:siddhis-as-obstacles"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.17-18", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.17-18"}, "paraphrase": "Of the 72,000 doors only the suṣumnā — the power of Śambhu — is useful; the others are useless.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:nadis"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.26-28", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.26-28"}, "paraphrase": "Liberation comes if the guru himself is pleased; restraining the breath at the ādhāra the body trembles and the yogin dances.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.35-46", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.35-46"}, "paraphrase": "The suṣumnā is praised as the supreme tīrtha — greater than Gaṅgā, Maṇikarṇikā, Śrīśaila, Vārāṇasī and Kedāra; a thousand horse-sacrifices are not worth a sixteenth of it; it is the supreme japa and meditation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:inner-tirthas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.58-61", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.58-61"}, "paraphrase": "A moving mind is saṃsāra, a still mind liberation; the unmanī state is beyond merit and sin.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:unmani"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.62-66", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.62-66"}, "paraphrase": "The mind looking at the mind: the ten signs (pratyaya) — bindu, nāda, kalā, light, sun, moon, pole-star, star, the peaceful and what is beyond — make him lord of yogins.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.71-73", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.71-73"}, "paraphrase": "Attention to nāda destroys vāsanās; nāda is bindu, and bindu is mind.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:nada", "cpt:bindu"], "practices": ["prc:nadanusandhana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.76-79", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.76-79"}, "paraphrase": "Fire in wood appears by churning; the lamp in a pot shows when the pot breaks by the guru's word; the guru is the helmsman.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
